<section class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Contributing</h1>
    <p>Help build the archive — submit requests, documents, agency updates, or template improvements.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="container">
  <div class="prose">

    <h2>What you can submit</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A new public records request entry (with MuckRock link or direct filing details).</li>
      <li>An update to a pending request (status change, partial production, denial, etc.).</li>
      <li>A newly released document or production.</li>
      <li>A correction to agency metadata.</li>
      <li>A request template improvement.</li>
      <li>A link to a public agency policy, annual report, or official public document.</li>
      <li>A proposed neutral finding supported by primary-source documents.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to contribute via GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      The easiest way to contribute is a pull request against the
      <a href="https://github.com/QuisCustodietLincoln/site-src" target="_blank" rel="noopener">site-src repository</a>.
      See the <a href="https://github.com/QuisCustodietLincoln/site-src/blob/main/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">README</a>
      for step-by-step instructions on updating requests, adding documents, or creating a new agency profile.
    </p>
    <p>Use the pull request template below when opening a PR:</p>

  </div>

  <pre class="pr-template">## Contribution type
- [ ] New records request
- [ ] Request status update
- [ ] Released document
- [ ] Agency profile update
- [ ] Correction
- [ ] Template improvement
- [ ] Other

## Agency / jurisdiction

## Source URL or attached record

## Date obtained or published

## Proposed factual description

## Primary-source citation
(Identify the specific document, page, row, or section.)

## Privacy review
- [ ] I reviewed this submission for personal contact information.
- [ ] I did not include raw plate data, plate numbers, travel/location histories, or sensitive investigative information.
- [ ] I preserved agency redactions.
- [ ] I understand contributions may be edited, rejected, or redacted before publication.
- [ ] I lawfully obtained or accessed all submitted materials.</pre>

  <div class="prose">

    <h2>Contribute by email</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="email-callout">
    <strong>Email intake</strong>
    <a href="mailto:submissions@alprnebraska.org">submissions@alprnebraska.org</a>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      For timely handling, emailed submissions should include the same information as the pull
      request template above: agency/jurisdiction, source URL or attached record, date obtained,
      a proposed factual description, and the primary-source citation.
    </p>

    <h2>Contributor expectations</h2>
    <p>
      Send public-records request materials, agency correspondence, released records, links to
      official policies or reports, or corrections. Do not send raw ALPR data, individual license
      plate information, live locations, investigative case material, sensitive personal
      information, or information obtained unlawfully.
    </p>
    <p>
      Submissions may be edited, rejected, or redacted before publication. Contributors retain
      responsibility for the lawful acquisition and submission of all materials.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
